# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canon Quill ignore rules
#
# Rule of thumb: the repo holds the *engine* only. Every byte of an author's
# book -- references pulled from Drive, extracted style corpora, bibles,
# drafts, chapters, exports, archives -- lives under a generated directory and
# must never be committed. Generated content is confined to `.canon-quill/`
# (active project) and `.canon-quill-archives/` (finished projects) so a single
# pair of rules covers anything added in the future.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Generated book content (NEVER commit) ---------------------------------
.canon-quill/
.canon-quill-archives/

# Defence in depth: catch generated content even if it escapes the dirs above.
**/artifacts/
**/chapters/
**/manuscript.*
**/style-corpus/
**/drive-cache/
*.docx
*.epub

# --- Secrets and credentials -----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
token.json
*token*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.secret.*
*.local.*

# --- Build output and dependencies -----------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Test and tooling output -----------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.vitest/

# --- Logs and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
tmp/
.tmp/

# --- OS / editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
